.Dd September 18, 2025
.Dt BASE64_ENCODE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm base64_encode
.Nd encode to Base64
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libbasse
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In base64.h
.Ft "void"
.Fo base64_encode
.Fa "const char *restrict in" "size_t inlen" "char *restrict out"
.Fa "size_t outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn base64_encode
function encodes
.Fa inlen
bytes from buffer
.Fa in
to Base64, as defined by RFC 4648, into buffer
.Fa out .
.Pp
If the space in bytes required to fully encode buffer
.Fa in
to Base64 is longer than
.Fa outlen ,
only
.Fa outlen
characters will be written to
.Fa out .
If
.Fa outlen
is larger than the length of the Base64-encoded form of
.Fa in ,
the
.Fn base64_encode
function additionally writes a terminating null byte
.Ql ( \e0 )
to buffer
.Fa out .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn base64_encode
function does not return a value.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The following program:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
